message.content:
This is a CBP ruling-type question: a costume kit with a headpiece, wings, and boot covers, all flimsy and sold for Halloween. Festive articles fall under heading 9505, and the costume accessories are classified there. Because the items are flimsy and not durable, they are not "wearing apparel" of chapters 61 or 62; note 1(e) to chapter 95 excludes fancy dress of textiles in chapters 61 and 62, but these flimsy items are not classifiable there. The set is therefore classified as a festive article in 9505.90.60 (other festive, carnival or other entertainment articles, other).

The HTS number is 9505.90.6000.

